{"agent_id":"pp3g-w1bb-code-analysis-task-issue-134-subissue-of-133-assess","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T03:56:34.688749021Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e4893281-311b-4929-8b82-de73fa9667c1","comment_uuid":"c6c55836-775d-4730-ba3d-6d2e939f44f6","author":"pp3g-w1bb-code-analysis-task-issue-134-subissue-of-133-assess","content":"## VERDICT — Repurposing crosslink for operator completion-notification\n\n**Bottom line: PRACTICAL — but the cheapest path is NOT the sentinel engine; it is a PostToolUse hook (pure Python, no Rust) or a narrow sentinel collect-pass extension. The sentinel is currently disabled in this repo, and its notification pipeline only covers sentinel-spawned agents. All file:function citations are from `/home/claude-code/projects/crosslink/crosslink/src/` (Rust) or `resources/claude/hooks/` (Python).**\n\n### 1) SENTINEL ENGINE — what it does, and the local-state gap\n\n- **Dispatch is GitHub-label-driven, not local-state-driven.** `sentinel/watch.rs::run_watch_loop` → `async_watch_loop` (watch.rs:200) runs a tokio `select!` loop multiplexing: (a) a poll timer of `interval_minutes * 60` s (default 10 min, watch.rs:206; backoff ×2 up to 8× on failure, watch.rs:326-331), (b) optional GitHub webhook events, (c) SIGTERM/SIGINT/stdin-close. Each tick calls `engine::run_oneshot` (engine.rs:26) → `poll_all_sources` (engine.rs:64), which instantiates only external adapters implementing the `Source::poll()` trait (sources/mod.rs:54-61): GitHubLabelSource, GitHubCISource, InternalHygieneSource, MaintenanceSweepSource, CpitdSource. **None of them observe local agent state** (`.worktrees/*/.kickoff-status`, tmux, docker). Dispatch decisions are label triage in `dispatch.rs::triage` (dispatch.rs:44) for `agent-todo: replicate|fix`.\n- **Completion detection ALREADY exists — for sentinel-spawned agents only.** `process_signal_batch` step 7 calls `collect::collect_completed` (engine.rs:313; collect.rs:46): it reads `db.get_pending_dispatches()` (db/sentinel.rs:192 — rows from the `sentinel_dispatches` table), checks each worktree's `.kickoff-status` (collect.rs:71), classifies via `classify_status` (collect.rs:366: DONE→success, FAILED/TIMEOUT→failure/exhausted), posts the GH result comment, files an `agent-exhausted` triage issue, and calls **`super::notify::notify_dispatch_completed` (collect.rs:153 → notify.rs:12)**, which POSTs Slack Block Kit or generic JSON webhooks (`{\"event\":\"sentinel.dispatch.completed\",...}`, notify.rs:123-133) via a curl subprocess (notify.rs:149).\n- **Could a local-state observer be added with small effort? YES — two options.** (a) Follow the `internal.rs` Source pattern (sources/internal.rs:146-168 — opens issues.db, emits `Signal`s) with a new `sources/local.rs` that scans `.worktrees/*/.kickoff-status` (logic already exists in `kickoff/monitor.rs::discover_agents`, monitor.rs:173-314; note it is `pub(super)` — needs `pub(crate)` for reuse), registered in `poll_all_sources` (engine.rs:64-102) + a new `SourcesConfig` field (config.rs:35-43). (b) Simpler: extend `collect::collect_completed` to also sweep non-sentinel worktrees and reuse the existing `notify_dispatch_completed` — ~80-150 LOC total.\n- **The real gap**: `insert_sentinel_dispatch` is called ONLY from `engine.rs:237`/`engine.rs:255`. Manually `kickoff run`-dispatched agents never enter `sentinel_dispatches`, so the existing collect+notify pipeline ignores them. Any repurpose must either write dispatch rows at kickoff launch (`kickoff/run.rs::run`, run.rs:17) or scan worktrees directly.\n\n### 2) EVENT SYSTEM — no agent-completion event; no events table\n\n- Events are NOT in issues.db (db/core.rs:165-423 tables: issues, labels, dependencies, comments, sessions, time_entries, relations, milestones, milestone_issues, token_usage, sentinel_runs, sentinel_dispatches — **no events table**). They are append-only NDJSON per-agent files `agents/{agent_id}/events.log` on git refs `refs/heads/crosslink/agents/<id>` (events.rs:1-7; `hub_v3.rs::append_event_to_ref`, hub_v3.rs:203), committed by `shared_writer` (`write_commit_push`, mutations.rs:178).\n- **There is NO 'kickoff agent completed' event.** The `Event` enum (events.rs:72-260) covers IssueCreated/LockClaimed/StatusChanged/CommentAdded/… — nothing about agents. The de-facto completion signal is `CommentAdded{kind: \"result\"}` (events.rs:170, `kind` field events.rs:178): agents post `--kind result` comments on completion, which land in their events.log. A watcher can detect completion by polling agent refs and parsing new `CommentAdded` with kind=\"result\" — the dashboard already polls refs this way for heartbeats (`server/watcher.rs::resolve_watch_target` watches `.git/refs/heads/crosslink/` recursively, watcher.rs:58-98).\n- **Subscription infra that exists**: `crosslink dashboard serve` runs a 5s poll loop (dashboard/poll.rs:53-93) + a WebSocket broadcast stream (`server/ws.rs`, `server/types.rs::WsEventType` variants: heartbeat, agent_status, issue_updated, lock_changed, execution_progress — types.rs:629-643) and already exposes each agent's `kickoff_status` (server/types.rs:406-408; handlers/agents.rs:293). No AgentCompleted variant exists; adding one is a small extension of `ws.rs`/`types.rs` + `watcher.rs::diff_and_broadcast`.\n- \"Tail crosslink/hub\": hub hydration goes through `RefHubSource` (locks_cmd.rs:263 → hub_source.rs); there is no follow/tail facility — only `sync` snapshots.\n\n### 3) HOOKS — post-action hook points exist (and one is already a notifier pattern)\n\n- `crosslink-guard.ts` (this repo's `.opencode/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts`) registers **only `tool.execute.before`** (line 855) — it is a pre-action guard, not a notify site. Adding `tool.execute.after` is possible but the plugin runs in the operator's opencode session, not the agent session, so it cannot see agent DONE writes.\n- **PostToolUse hooks ARE deployed** (resources/claude/hooks/): `heartbeat.py` fires after EVERY tool call in the agent session (throttled `crosslink heartbeat` every 120s) — this is the exact shape a completion-notify hook would take, and `post-edit-check.py` fires after Write|Edit. A new `completion-notify.py` (~30-60 LOC, Python) can run after the agent's final Write of `.kickoff-status` (content == \"DONE\"), then POST a webhook exactly like notify.rs does with curl. This is the **cheapest path: zero Rust changes**; only config (webhook URL) + one deployed hook.\n- Caveat: hooks run inside the agent worktree and only when the claude session is alive — a killed/timed-out agent writes no DONE (launch writes FAILED/RUNNING itself, launch.rs:648-665), so hook-based notify covers clean completion, not failure; container-mode wiring differs.\n\n### 4) CLI — no watch/event-stream command\n\n- There is **no `crosslink watch` or event-stream/tail command**. `sentinel watch` (main.rs:2108) is the sentinel daemon only. `kickoff logs` (monitor.rs:387) is a snapshot (events.log byte size + heartbeat + git log), not a follow. Closest existing always-on daemons: `sentinel watch`, `daemon run` (daemon.rs:111, 30s session/heartbeat flush), `dashboard serve` (dashboard/poll.rs), `mc` (main.rs:350). A new `crosslink watch` would be net-new CLI surface.\n\n### 5) ESTIMATE — cheapest repurposing paths, LOC, risks\n\n**Path B (cheapest — hook notify):** new `resources/claude/hooks/completion-notify.py` (~30-60 LOC) + config key + deploy hook in `crosslink init` (commands/init) + settings.json matcher. No Rust. Latency: instant (fires on the DONE write). Risk: agent-session-dependent, no failure-case coverage, container caveat.\n\n**Path A (sentinel local observer, ~150-300 LOC):** `sources/local.rs` (NEW ~150-250) + register in `poll_all_sources` (engine.rs:64) + config (config.rs) + optional `monitor.rs::discover_agents` visibility change; OR extend `collect.rs::collect_completed` (~80-150) and reuse `notify.rs` unchanged. Latency: poll interval (10 min default, ≥1 min). Reuses the complete notify pipeline. Risks below.\n\n**Path C (dashboard WS watcher, ~100-200 LOC):** extend `server/watcher.rs` + new `WsEventType::AgentCompleted` (types.rs) + `ws.rs`; requires `dashboard serve` always-on. Best for a UI destination; overkill for a simple operator ping.\n\n**Risks (all paths):**\n1. **Sentinel disabled here**: ASES `hook-config.json` has `\"sentinel\": {\"enabled\": false}` — Path A is inert until the sentinel daemon is enabled AND `sentinel watch` runs (PID file, watch.rs:17-64).\n2. **Latency/backoff**: 10-min (min 1) interval; ×8 backoff after failures stretches to 80 min (watch.rs:326-331).\n3. **DB semantics**: `sentinel_dispatches` excludes manual kickoffs (insert only at engine.rs:237); direct `Database::open(issues.db)` inside the sentinel cycle (watch.rs:388) contends with CLI/SharedWriter writes; stale locks are already observed in this repo (5 stale).\n4. **Dedup/idempotency**: `SeenSet` + DB dedup + `gh_comment_already_posted` (collect.rs:10) are tuned for GH-label signals; local-completion signals need their own reference semantics to avoid duplicate notifications.\n5. **Worktree races**: `collect.rs:64-67` marks missing worktrees \"orphaned\" — cleanup-before-notify can swallow notifications.\n6. **notify.rs uses curl** (notify.rs:149) — curl must exist; generic webhook/Slack only (no desktop/terminal channel today).\n7. **Hook path fragility**: only clean-completion, local-tmux launches; no failure/container coverage.\n\n**Recommended**: Path B for an immediate, near-zero-effort operator ping (add `completion-notify.py` beside `heartbeat.py`), with Path A as the durable Rust option if failure-case + sentinel-dispatched coverage is required. Avoid Path D (new Event variant + reducer + migration) — highest cost for no benefit over B.","created_at":"2026-08-03T03:56:34.681862285Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:Sfu6q1cx1SU8enDz/K+FdP03v3AD2Xk9KWJCa14HzmM","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgmEKVgA4YkEchP1Vsu18cf0kFV4LAUEhOyIlBIby+4qIAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAho/DLOPU3UvUp4irEalwu5yrNdSm6tqb+grV/lFVniu+HdDl8jJheLREspB1FaLf/P1cTt6RWoPabolsCCqmAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:Sfu6q1cx1SU8enDz/K+FdP03v3AD2Xk9KWJCa14HzmM","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgmEKVgA4YkEchP1Vsu18cf0kFV4LAUEhOyIlBIby+4qIAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCD2qki9ArS2W3y8ycupbDZ+tb4LAJFcQAku4TyFt7QxDliGPQxP7ByTuGv5okkT4hjKpaYcxBPLSicDdsMWXA8="}
